><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Pietinen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rohan</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Sellers</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Speizer</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name><name><surname>Willett</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolk</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alcohol intake and colorectal cancer: a pooled analysis of 8 cohort studies</article-title><source>Ann Inter Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>140</volume><fpage>603</fpage><lpage>613</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Ann Inter Med||140|603||bib7|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cochran</surname><given-names>WG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The combination of estimates from different experiments</article-title><source>Biometrics</source><year>1954</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>129</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Biometrics||10|101||bib8|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regression models and life-tables</article-title><source>J R Statist Soc, Series (B)</source><year>1972</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J R Statist Soc, Series (B)||34|187||bib9|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cramer</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Welch</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Determinants of ovarian cancer risk. II. Inferences regarding pathogenesis</article-title><source>J Nat Cancer Institute</source><year>1983</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>717</fpage><lpage>721</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Nat Cancer Institute||71|717||bib10|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DerSimonian</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Laird</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Meta-analysis in clinical trials</article-title><source>Controlled Clin Trials</source><year>1986</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>188</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Controlled Clin Trials||7|177||bib11|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Durrleman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Flexible regression models with cubic splines</article-title><source>Statist Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>551</fpage><lpage>561</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Statist Med||8|551||bib12|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Epicure software</collab></person-group><article-title/><source>EPICURE user's guide: the PEANUTS program</source><year>1993</year><publisher-name>Seattle: Hirosoft</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flagg</surname><given-names>EW</given-names></name><name><surname>Coates</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Calle</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name><name><surname>Potischman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Thun</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Validation of the American Cancer Soci